ppet\":\" ... The winner was Douglas Stuart for his debut novel Shuggie Bain, which had been rejected by more than 30 publishers.\\n\\n2021's small-scale ceremony, once again impacted by COVID-19, saw South African writer Damon Galgut, who had been shortlisted in 2003 and 2010, win the prize ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d28\"},\"ref\":\"d28\",\"snippet\":\" ... Booker Prize. Morrall was also shortlisted for British Newcomer of the Year 2003. Her fourth novel, The Man who Disappeared, was selected for the TV Book Club 2010. In 2012 The Roundabout Man was released to critical acclaim.\\n\\nHer novels have been translated into many languages across the ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.ruberybookaward.com/judges.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d29\"},\"ref\":\"d29\",\"snippet\":\" ... to his fiction because he narrates his novels as if he were someone both wise and ignorant.\\\"\\n\\nMore than two million copies of Saramago's books have been sold in Portugal alone and his work has been translated into 25 languages. A proponent of libertarian communism, Saramago criticized ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jos%C3%A9_Saramago\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d30\"},\"ref\":\"d30\",\"snippet\":\" ... prize more than once), Praiseworthy wins the UK's James Tait Black Prize and is shortlisted for the Dublin Literary Award and the Climate Fiction Prize, among others. Marosia Castaldi's The Hunger of Women wins the ALTA Prize for Prose (for the best translation from any language ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.andotherstories.org/about-us/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d13\"},\"ref\":\"d13\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 2010 he was shortlisted again for the Scotiabank Giller Prize for his sixth novel The Matter with Morris.\\n\\nOct. 25 Alissa York - Fauna\\n\\nAlissa York is the author of three novels: Fauna (2010), Effigy(2007) and Mercy (200?) as well as a collection of short fiction Any ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.yorku.ca/laps/huma/canadian-writers/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d31\"},\"ref\":\"d31\",\"snippet\":\" ... exuberant, coruscating translation.\\n\\n\\\"This is a luminous novel of India and Partition, but one whose spellbinding brio and fierce compassion weaves youth and age, male and female, family and nation into a kaleidoscopic whole.\\\"\\n\\nThe International Booker Prize 2022 Shortlist\\n\\n| Title | Author | Translator | Original Language | Author Residence | Publisher ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2022/05/geetanjali-shree-and-daisy-rockwell-win-the-international-booker-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d3\"},\"ref\":\"d3\",\"snippet\":\" ... Her books have been translated into more than fifty languages and have won dozens of international awards, including the Orange Prize, the Guardian Fiction Prize, the Lannan Award for Fiction, and the Commonwealth Poetry Prize for the Americas. Among many other honours, she is a Royal … Read More ... \",\"title\":\"https://griffinpoetryprize.com/judges/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d32\"},\"ref\":\"d32\",\"snippet\":\" ... Neel Mukherjee is the author of three novels: A Life Apart (2010), which won the Writers' Guild of Great Britain Award for Best Fiction Book; The Lives of Others (2014), which was shortlisted for the Man Booker Prize and the Costa Best Novel Award, and won the Royal ... \",\"title\":\"https://pen.org/meet-the-2021-literary-awards-judges/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"438869ffb33709bee18fce9ae60951b089414aac8861e4a32e9791521dfa172e\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"fbd1b2f663d5c53e9a0cddca7ffb5632c90805e246f00c7bc600e40b530a34f9\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"novel translated 25 languages prize shortlist 2010s\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_1367da83d13347f9a58c86ae"},{"content":"The International Booker Prize is a strong candidate — it was created in the 2000s (2005 as the Man Booker International Prize) and is given to books in translation. Let me reconsider the structure:\n\n- Award created in 2000s → International Booker Prize (established 2005)\n- Book A: contender for this award, translated into 25+ languages, published in the 2010s\n- In the year Book A was published, Book B won the award\n- Book B was released the preceding year\n- Author of Book B born in city where author of Book A grew up\n\nLet me search for International Booker Prize winners and contenders in the 2010s.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"International Booker Prize winners 2010s list\", \"Man Booker International Prize shortlist 2010s translated 25 languages\", \"International Booker Prize contender translated over 25 languages 2010s\"], \"top_k\": 8}","name":"search"},"id":"call_cdbbb4a984524bcf9c1739ba","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": \"\\\"Man Booker International Prize\\\" winner 2013 2014 2015 2016\\\",