,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d24\"},\"ref\":\"d24\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 2018, the Polish novelist was recognized for \\\"Flights,\\\" which she calls a \\\"constellation novel,\\\" owing to its fragmentary form and genre-defying style, and which won that year's Man Booker Prize. \\\"Drive Your Plow Over the Bones of the Dead,\\\" her latest novel to be translated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.newyorker.com/books/page-turner/the-2019-national-book-awards-longlist-translated-literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d43\"},\"ref\":\"d43\",\"snippet\":\" ... Carey has won the Miles Franklin Award three times and is frequently named as Australia's next contender for the Nobel Prize in Literature. Carey is one of only five writers to have won the Booker Prize twice—the others being J. G. Farrell, J. M. Coetzee, Hilary ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.goodreads.com/topic/show/22141667-winners-of-the-miles-franklin-literary-award\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d31\"},\"ref\":\"d31\",\"snippet\":\" ... In London, Geetanjali Shree and Daisy Rockwell Win the 2022 International Booker Prize\\nauthor: Porter Anderson\\ndate: 2022-05-26\\n---\\n'Tomb of Sand' is the first novel translated from an Indian language to win the award. Shree and Rockwell split the International Booker's £50,000 purse.\\n\\nBy ... \",\"title\":\"https://publishingperspectives.com/2022/05/geetanjali-shree-and-daisy-rockwell-win-the-international-booker-prize/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d16\"},\"ref\":\"d16\",\"snippet\":\" ... The Future is the translation of Leroux's French-language novel L'Avenir.\\n\\nLeroux is a writer, translator and journalist from Montreal. She was shortlisted for the 2016 Scotiabank Giller Prize for The Party Wall, which is an English translation of her French-language short story collection Le ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.cbc.ca/books/the-top-20-canadian-books-of-2024-so-far-1.7252475\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d17\"},\"ref\":\"d17\",\"snippet\":\" ... It was nominated for both the Man Booker Prize (now known as the Booker Prize) and the National Book Award and earned Lahiri the 2015 DSC Prize for South Asian Literature, a prize established in 2010 by infrastructure developers DSC Limited to honor the achievements of South Asian ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.britannica.com/biography/Jhumpa-Lahiri\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d36\"},\"ref\":\"d36\",\"snippet\":\" ... Since 2005, a second prize, the International Booker Prize, has also been awarded, which since 2016 has gone to the best work in translation.\\n\\nThese 70 judges were 57 percent men; 75 percent English; 16 percent Irish, Scottish, or Welsh; 10 percent other nationalities; and 99 percent white ... \",\"title\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10837049/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"b3fb9c6c998c9dcc739aaf062a5607d64af474e33a7fe74c4a77604eb00114c6\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"fede07e31180d9e5ecdad1fff8b56c5987e67d63e1afec7f219d86af2b6ee4c8\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"International Booker Prize contender translated over 25 languages 2010s\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_cdbbb4a984524bcf9c1739ba"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"blocks_finish\":true,\"code\":\"arguments_invalid\",\"executed\":false,\"message\":\"search: invalid fields near ['queries']; follow the supplied schema\",\"ok\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_4d5408cc66b348b6ab5de3b2"},{"content":"I have a strong lead. The International Booker Prize was established in 2005 (2000s). Let me look at the key clue: Chigozie Obioma's novels \"The Fishermen\" (2015) and \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) were shortlisted for the Booker Prize and translated into 30 languages.\n\nLet me reconsider the structure. The award created in the 2000s could be the Man Booker International Prize (2005). Let me check the winners and look at the connection more carefully. Let me read the Booker Prize page and search for more specific information.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d40\"}","name":"read"},"id":"call_8114a55af9ca43cdb529d88e","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Man Booker International Prize winners 2016 2017 2018 2019\", \"International Booker Prize winner 2016 The Discomfort of Evening\", \"International Booker Prize 2017 winner Flights Olga Tokarczuk\"], \"top_k\": 8}","name":"search"},"id":"call_31b81c9a760646edb5766a93","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d40\",\"document_chars\":17355,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e1\",\"sha256\":\"79767844ce2071fc5dcf3fb0e64d0cade0ba154ef0fc324d0054c1c767e63138\",\"snapshot\":\"90019ca46504785f620ef12f36abae20080c8c3bc7809053339e4beaa4deb2fd\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: ADVISORS\\ndate: 2022-01-01\\n---\\nADVISORS\\n\\nAdvisors\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated for two dozen prizes for fiction. He was named one of Foreign Policy's 100 Leading Global Thinkers in 2015 and served as a judge of the Booker prize in 2021. He is the Helen S. Lanier Distinguished Professor of English and Creative Writing at the University of Georgia, and the program director of the Oxbelly Writers retreat. His third novel, The Road to the Country, was published in 2024.\\n\\nProgram Manager\\n\\nRosie is a production and event manager based in Athens, Greece, with extensive experience in coordinating high-profile film festivals and cultural events. She holds a degree in Communication, Media and Culture from Athens and pursued further studies in Art History in Paris, culminating in a Master's in Culture & Tourism from Université Paris 1 Panthéon-Sorbonne. Her professional experience includes collaborations with cultural organizations and festivals worldwide, including UNESCO in New York, the Rolex Art Festival, Les Rencontres d'Arles Photo Festival among others. Since 2018, she has served as Festival Coordinator and Special Events Manager for the French Film Festival of Greece, and since 2022, she has been the Head of Production for the Athens International Children's Film Festival. Driven by a deep passion for cultural engagement and sustainable tourism, she continually seeks innovative ways to connect communities through the arts. In her free time, she enjoys playing music and gardening.\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationaler Literaturpreis, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated for two dozen prizes for fiction. He was a judge of the Booker prize in 2021. He is the Helen S. Lanier Professor of Creative Writing and English at the University of Georgia, and the program director of the Oxbelly Fiction Writers program. His third novel, The Road to the Country, will be published in 2024.\\n\\nProgram Manager\\n\\nKaterina Papanikolopoulos joined Faliro House in 2022 as Manager of Special Projects – a position that evolved into her role acting as the 2024 Oxbelly Retreat, Fiction Writers Program Manager. Following her graduation from UCLA (Summa Cum Laude, Art History), Papanikolopoulos founded the non-profit Athens Design Forum (ADF), a platform that advocates for overlooked and generative design histories interwoven with global labor and migration pa\"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":3000,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_8114a55af9ca43cdb529d88e"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d20\"},\"ref\":\"d20\",\"snippet\":\" ... the Man Booker Prize (2002–2019), is a prestigious literary award conferred each year for the best single work of sustained fiction written in the English language, which was published in the United Kingdom or Ireland. The winner of the Booker Prize receives , as well as international publicity ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d33\"},\"ref\":\"d33\",\"snippet\":\" ... Award, 2017\\n\\n- Raymond Chandler Award, 2017\\n\\n- Academy Board of Directors' Tribute, 2018\\n\\n- UCD Ulysses Medal, 2018\\n\\n- Adrienne Clarkson Prize for Global Citizenship, 2018\\n\\n- Order of the Companions of Honour, 2018\\n\\n- LARB/UCR Lifetime Achievement Award, 2019\\n\\n- VH1 Tr